20:45.100 --> 20:50.140
And this is governed by restriction maps and admissible gluing.

20:50.340 --> 20:51.520
Admissible gluing.

20:51.780 --> 20:52.080
Okay.

20:52.180 --> 20:52.980
Let's look at that.

20:52.980 --> 20:59.440
Because how do you take billions of fully autonomous independent cells and bind them together

20:59.440 --> 21:04.880
to form a functioning liver without destroying the autonomy of the individual cells?

21:05.620 --> 21:06.980
That's the million dollar question.

21:06.980 --> 21:14.500
And the answer is that an embedding of a lower level stalk into a higher level stalk is only

21:14.500 --> 21:22.280
admissible if the lower level can maintain its own local endomorphism loop while simultaneously

21:22.280 --> 21:25.880
exporting outputs that maintain the higher level loop.

21:25.880 --> 21:32.840
Furthermore, the overarching constraints imposed by the higher level must not crush the essential

21:32.840 --> 21:34.780
viable loops of the lower level.

21:35.180 --> 21:38.380
It's a very precise topological mutualism.

21:38.660 --> 21:38.920
Okay.

