160 hours a week with zero resources...

22:17.780 --> 22:20.320
The local loop of the accounting department just collapses.

22:20.920 --> 22:21.240
Right.

22:21.840 --> 22:25.660
The global structure destroyed the local stalk.

22:26.160 --> 22:32.580
Admissible gluing requires that both the local cellular loop and the global organismic loop

22:32.580 --> 22:34.420
thrive simultaneously.

22:34.420 --> 22:36.320
That is a perfect analogy.

22:37.060 --> 22:42.860
But biological reality rarely achieves perfect mathematical idealization.

22:43.060 --> 22:43.700
Of course not.

22:43.800 --> 22:47.100
Which requires the introduction of partial admissibility.

22:47.460 --> 22:53.380
This is represented by the parameter alpha, which scales continuously from zero to one.

22:53.780 --> 22:58.720
So if alpha equals exactly one, you have perfect, robust health.

22:58.900 --> 22:59.200
Right.

22:59.200 --> 23:04.920
Every cellular loop is perfectly glued to the tissue loop, the tissue to the organ, the organ

23:04.920 --> 23:05.660
to the organism.

23:05.760 --> 23:07.520
But what happens when it's not one?

23:07.920 --> 23:13.220
When alpha falls between zero and one, the system enters a state of compensated pathology.

23:13.820 --> 23:14.940
Compensated pathology.

23:15.040 --> 23:15.820
What does that look like?

23:15.920 --> 23:21.360
Well, the restriction maps preserve enough essential loops to prevent immediate systemic collapse,

23:21.640 --> 23:25.200
but non-essential or localized loops degrade.

23:25.200 --> 23:30.100
The system continues to operate, but it's carrying thermodynamic debt.

23:30.660 --> 23:36.740
This mathematical state corresponds exactly to subclinical disease, chronic stress, or just

23:36.740 --> 23:39.260
the slow systemic degradation of aging.

23:39.820 --> 23:45.940
The organism is functioning, but the mathematical robustness of the gluing is compromised.

23:46.500 --> 23:49.560
And alpha equal to zero is terminal.

23:49.560 --> 23:50.080
Yes.

