Let me try to put this into an analogy.

29:58.540 --> 30:04.300
Think of the CLIO descent like attempting to solve a wildly complex Rubik's Cube.

30:04.480 --> 30:04.680
Sure.

30:04.900 --> 30:11.540
But this is a biological Rubik's Cube that is actively being scrambled by the surrounding

30:11.540 --> 30:12.860
thermodynamic entropy.

30:13.160 --> 30:13.480
Right.

30:13.740 --> 30:19.160
So the CLIO operator represents the continuous algorithmic twisting of the rows,

30:19.940 --> 30:22.260
scanning millions of microconfigurations,

30:22.880 --> 30:27.000
searching for the exact sequence of moves that aligns the colors.

30:27.000 --> 30:28.860
Minimizing the obstruction.

30:29.000 --> 30:29.480
Exactly.

30:29.940 --> 30:34.880
So that the local constraints harmonize and the global structure locks back into place.

30:35.080 --> 30:37.500
That is a very apt way to describe it.

30:37.840 --> 30:41.920
It is a process of gradient descent toward constraint harmonization.

30:42.380 --> 30:43.200
So elegant.

